mojo-bstr is a Mojo port of the current goostr byte-string API by Seth Stadick.

The goostr source states that its search algorithms derive from memchr 2.8.3.
Byte-string/UTF-8 behavior follows bstr 1.13.1. Both projects are by Andrew
Gallant. The original MIT license and copyright notices are retained in LICENSE.

tests/oracle and tests/differential.py derive from goostr's test harness.
Benchmark protocol and verification conventions derive from goostr's
Rust/bstr comparison and memchr/rebar benchmark harnesses.

Upstream references:
https://github.com/sstadick/goostr
https://github.com/BurntSushi/bstr
https://github.com/BurntSushi/memchr
https://github.com/BurntSushi/rebar
